WEBVTT

1
00:00:38.997 --> 00:00:40.957
FEMALE NARRATOR: <i>Home.</i>

2
00:00:45.837 --> 00:00:49.841
<i>It's the place where childhood</i>
<i>and memory live together.</i>

3
00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:05.356
<i>But the home of my childhood is changing.</i>

4
00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.616
<i>The ice we depend on is melting away.</i>

5
00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:28.421
<i>My cub and I are in uncharted waters.</i>

6
00:02:12.882 --> 00:02:17.345
<i>I was born in an ice cave,</i>
<i>high in the mountains.</i>

7
00:02:35.363 --> 00:02:40.493
<i>But the frozen ocean, the sea ice,</i>
<i>was our home.</i>

8
00:02:50.211 --> 00:02:52.755
<i>Here is where my earliest memories are.</i>

9
00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.884
<i>Playing with my best friend,</i>

10
00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:58.469
<i>my twin brother.</i>

11
00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.364
<i>And she was never far from us.</i>

12
00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:22.118
<i>Our protector.</i>

13
00:03:23.411 --> 00:03:24.704
<i>Our mother.</i>

14
00:03:50.146 --> 00:03:53.775
<i>I was stronger than my brother.</i>
<i>More curious.</i>

15
00:03:56.194 --> 00:03:58.947
<i>But he was the independent one.</i>

16
00:04:00.156 --> 00:04:02.158
<i>I always followed Mom's lead.</i>

17
00:04:08.331 --> 00:04:11.793
<i>And there was a whole world</i>
<i>she wanted to show us.</i>

18
00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.243
<i>There was so much to learn here.</i>

19
00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:52.542
<i>She was our only teacher.</i>

20
00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.838
(MOTHER BEAR GRUNTS)

21
00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:59.340
<i>I copied everything she did.</i>

22
00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.926
<i>I didn't know it, but we were hunting...</i>

23
00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.096
<i>for something.</i>

24
00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.315
(SNIFFS)

25
00:05:58.941 --> 00:06:00.485
<i>For a smell.</i>

26
00:06:02.362 --> 00:06:06.032
-(SNIFFS)
<i>-A smell under the ice.</i>

27
00:06:24.092 --> 00:06:26.844
<i>Whatever it was, it smelled good.</i>

28
00:06:37.855 --> 00:06:40.691
<i>My brother was ready to attack, too...</i>

29
00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.363
-(GRUNTS)
<i>-Me, usually.</i>

30
00:06:52.954 --> 00:06:55.915
<i>Mom just kept pounding through the ice.</i>

31
00:06:57.291 --> 00:06:59.043
<i>I wanted to help her, but...</i>

32
00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:01.671
<i>I was busy.</i>

33
00:07:11.013 --> 00:07:15.101
<i>Then suddenly,</i>
<i>the whole thing became clear.</i>

34
00:07:19.439 --> 00:07:21.899
<i>We were seal hunting.</i>

35
00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:27.780
<i>Well, Mom was seal hunting.</i>

36
00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.926
<i>She was our hero.</i>

37
00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:52.263
<i>We would've followed her anywhere.</i>

38
00:07:58.686 --> 00:08:00.521
<i>And we needed to.</i>

39
00:08:18.873 --> 00:08:24.670
<i>Male bears spend all winter roaming</i>
<i>the ice, and are very, very hungry.</i>

40
00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:35.181
<i>My brother and I would make an easy meal.</i>

41
00:08:38.809 --> 00:08:43.439
<i>So Mom led us to the ice edge,</i>
<i>to the open ocean.</i>

42
00:08:49.028 --> 00:08:51.656
<i>The problem was,</i>
<i>we didn't know how to swim.</i>

43
00:08:53.991 --> 00:08:56.619
<i>We'd never even been in the water before.</i>

44
00:09:06.504 --> 00:09:08.256
<i>It was freezing.</i>

45
00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:13.636
<i>And the only dry land in sight was Mom.</i>

46
00:09:27.191 --> 00:09:28.442
(BARKING)

47
00:09:30.403 --> 00:09:33.364
<i>She knew we weren't going to learn</i>
<i>to swim like this.</i>

48
00:09:44.792 --> 00:09:47.670
<i>And there was good reason</i>
<i>to keep paddling.</i>

49
00:09:54.885 --> 00:09:56.053
(GRUNTS)

50
00:10:01.642 --> 00:10:07.648
<i>Finally, a place to rest... I thought.</i>

51
00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.485
<i>And I was wrong.</i>

52
00:10:23.581 --> 00:10:29.503
<i>When my brother and I could swim no more,</i>
<i>she led us ashore.</i>

53
00:10:32.757 --> 00:10:37.011
<i>I've never been happier to be bitten</i>
<i>and tugged by the scruff of the neck.</i>

54
00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:53.402
<i>We were safe.</i>

55
00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:57.156
<i>Now we could rest.</i>

56
00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:11.712
<i>Every spring,</i>
<i>as the sun climbs higher in the sky,</i>

57
00:11:12.171 --> 00:11:15.049
<i>the days become longer and warmer.</i>

58
00:11:35.611 --> 00:11:39.490
<i>Our world of solid ice</i>
<i>starts to break apart.</i>

59
00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:47.707
<i>I learned this was the natural way</i>
<i>of things.</i>

60
00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:58.467
<i>But this new, broken, shifting ground</i>
<i>was hard to get used to.</i>

61
00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:06.475
<i>Keeping up with Mom was not easy.</i>

62
00:12:20.489 --> 00:12:25.077
<i>One small step for her</i>
<i>was a giant leap for us.</i>

63
00:12:36.756 --> 00:12:43.262
<i>And now, for the first time, she would</i>
<i>leave my brother and me on our own.</i>

64
00:12:50.394 --> 00:12:52.146
<i>She had a new mission.</i>

65
00:12:58.861 --> 00:13:05.493
<i>I watched her as she silently disappeared,</i>
<i>becoming one with the ice floes.</i>

66
00:13:07.578 --> 00:13:09.288
<i>Master of the stalk.</i>

67
00:13:19.340 --> 00:13:24.011
<i>Mom knew, from experience,</i>
<i>her only chance at grabbing a seal</i>

68
00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:26.764
<i>was when it was up on an ice floe.</i>

69
00:13:29.850 --> 00:13:33.229
<i>As soon as it was in the water,</i>
<i>she wouldn't be able to catch it.</i>

70
00:16:35.703 --> 00:16:37.413
<i>There wasn't much for us to do.</i>

71
00:16:38.914 --> 00:16:41.959
<i>We just waited for her to return.</i>

72
00:16:52.886 --> 00:16:54.346
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

73
00:16:56.223 --> 00:17:00.728
<i>But she didn't return.</i>
<i>She kept on hunting.</i>

74
00:18:33.237 --> 00:18:35.989
<i>Mom caught many seals that first summer.</i>

75
00:18:37.032 --> 00:18:40.285
<i>We were well fed and wanted for nothing.</i>

76
00:19:03.183 --> 00:19:08.981
<i>Back then, life on our frozen</i>
<i>ocean home felt secure.</i>

77
00:19:26.999 --> 00:19:32.212
<i>Today, the sea ice we once called home</i>
<i>is disappearing.</i>

78
00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:49.354
<i>Seals need the sea ice to breed.</i>

79
00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:01.992
<i>We need seals to hunt.</i>

80
00:20:13.045 --> 00:20:14.838
<i>We are ice bears.</i>

81
00:20:21.303 --> 00:20:23.889
<i>How are we to survive without ice?</i>

82
00:20:41.031 --> 00:20:45.035
<i>Our mother kept us safe and warm</i>
<i>that first long winter.</i>

83
00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:51.416
<i>Other than the lights</i>
<i>that danced in the sky,</i>

84
00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:55.379
<i>it was total darkness</i>
<i>for half of the year.</i>

85
00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:07.266
<i>I thought the sun had gone forever.</i>

86
00:21:09.393 --> 00:21:12.187
<i>I remember the day it finally reappeared.</i>

87
00:21:52.019 --> 00:21:55.230
<i>My brother and I loved the sunshine.</i>

88
00:21:59.609 --> 00:22:01.778
<i>We could go and explore again.</i>

89
00:22:02.779 --> 00:22:06.283
(BRAYING)

90
00:22:08.327 --> 00:22:11.246
<i>But Mom was going to put</i>
<i>all that energy to use.</i>

91
00:22:12.289 --> 00:22:14.875
<i>She had a busy spring planned for us.</i>

92
00:22:23.759 --> 00:22:28.680
<i>Spring is when we need to catch nearly all</i>
<i>our food for the entire year...</i>

93
00:22:29.473 --> 00:22:30.724
<i>and quickly.</i>

94
00:22:32.225 --> 00:22:37.189
<i>Soon, most of the sea ice will disappear,</i>
<i>and with it, the seals.</i>

95
00:22:52.245 --> 00:22:55.165
<i>This year, Mom would expect a lot from us.</i>

96
00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:00.712
<i>She wanted us to really understand</i>
<i>seal hunting.</i>

97
00:23:04.383 --> 00:23:07.803
<i>No more spectating in between</i>
<i>wrestling matches.</i>

98
00:23:37.999 --> 00:23:41.962
<i>I also learned to never drop my guard.</i>

99
00:23:43.505 --> 00:23:47.175
(GRUMBLING)

100
00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:04.067
<i>Males were an ever-present threat.</i>

101
00:24:06.945 --> 00:24:10.907
<i>And this one caught us</i>
<i>completely by surprise.</i>

102
00:24:22.169 --> 00:24:26.673
<i>He was hungry, determined, and relentless.</i>

103
00:24:27.340 --> 00:24:28.925
(HUFFING)

104
00:24:42.898 --> 00:24:45.984
<i>There is no safe distance</i>
<i>from a male ice bear.</i>

105
00:24:48.028 --> 00:24:50.447
<i>But there is safe ice.</i>

106
00:24:51.948 --> 00:24:54.326
<i>And Mom knew how to find it.</i>

107
00:24:57.954 --> 00:25:02.459
<i>She followed the cracks that led</i>
<i>to the edge of the sea ice.</i>

108
00:25:06.922 --> 00:25:11.051
<i>It was so thin here, a large male bear</i>
<i>would fall right through.</i>

109
00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:21.853
<i>Most importantly, for my brother and me,</i>

110
00:25:23.563 --> 00:25:25.190
<i>we could play together.</i>

111
00:25:36.826 --> 00:25:41.331
<i>In those days, every moment out on</i>
<i>the sea ice taught us new lessons.</i>

112
00:25:45.669 --> 00:25:47.629
<i>About the different kinds of ice,</i>

113
00:25:51.258 --> 00:25:52.926
<i>the different thicknesses,</i>

114
00:25:54.469 --> 00:25:58.139
<i>how to plan the perfect belly-flop attack.</i>

115
00:26:04.437 --> 00:26:05.897
(BOTH GRUNTING)

116
00:26:29.254 --> 00:26:32.757
<i>It was an afternoon of pure relaxation.</i>

117
00:26:36.720 --> 00:26:40.432
<i>Plus, some extra seal-hunting practice</i>
<i>for my brother.</i>

118
00:27:04.247 --> 00:27:07.208
<i>A quick roll in the snow to dry our fur...</i>

119
00:27:10.462 --> 00:27:12.213
<i>And we were on the move again.</i>

120
00:27:27.228 --> 00:27:29.981
<i>We did grow a lot more confident</i>
<i>that spring.</i>

121
00:27:37.864 --> 00:27:41.451
<i>But Mom was still the center of our world.</i>

122
00:28:36.214 --> 00:28:39.592
<i>Today, there is little time for play.</i>

123
00:28:47.934 --> 00:28:51.104
<i>All of our energy is spent</i>
<i>searching for food.</i>

124
00:29:04.242 --> 00:29:08.037
<i>I want to teach my daughter</i>
<i>where to find seals.</i>

125
00:29:09.497 --> 00:29:14.377
<i>But the old places I was shown</i>
<i>are harder and harder to find.</i>

126
00:29:40.904 --> 00:29:45.950
<i>When summer came around again, the ice</i>
<i>seemed different than the year before.</i>

127
00:29:51.831 --> 00:29:55.668
<i>It felt hotter. And the melt came earlier.</i>

128
00:30:06.179 --> 00:30:10.558
<i>But the ice break-up allowed</i>
<i>fresh prey into our home.</i>

129
00:30:11.643 --> 00:30:14.562
<i>And these were not the seals</i>
<i>we'd come to know.</i>

130
00:30:20.944 --> 00:30:22.529
<i>Beluga whales.</i>

131
00:30:28.993 --> 00:30:32.038
<i>I had never seen a beluga whale before.</i>

132
00:30:40.171 --> 00:30:41.381
<i>Mom had, though.</i>

133
00:30:44.634 --> 00:30:47.929
<i>And she was set on</i>
<i>bringing one home for dinner.</i>

134
00:31:03.570 --> 00:31:06.781
<i>Catching prey in the water</i>
<i>is incredibly hard.</i>

135
00:31:14.455 --> 00:31:19.377
<i>But she was persistent. We needed to eat.</i>

136
00:32:03.963 --> 00:32:07.967
<i>Finally, one swam straight at her.</i>

137
00:32:27.612 --> 00:32:29.530
<i>It got away.</i>

138
00:32:30.823 --> 00:32:36.037
<i>But she was teaching us every chance</i>
<i>at food was worth taking.</i>

139
00:32:48.675 --> 00:32:52.345
<i>In summer,</i>
<i>the sun never sets for half the year.</i>

140
00:33:00.019 --> 00:33:04.691
<i>The unending daylight</i>
<i>brings a great wave of new life.</i>

141
00:33:36.055 --> 00:33:40.309
<i>Everyone rushes to raise their families</i>
<i>in the warm summer sun.</i>

142
00:34:07.211 --> 00:34:12.300
<i>Even with all this new life, summer is</i>
<i>always a season of hardship for us.</i>

143
00:34:14.093 --> 00:34:16.846
<i>You needed to take every opportunity.</i>

144
00:34:19.849 --> 00:34:20.850
(SNORTS)

145
00:34:24.812 --> 00:34:28.191
<i>The harbor seals were so tempting.</i>

146
00:34:31.819 --> 00:34:35.281
<i>But Mom had no ice floes</i>
<i>to help her hunt now.</i>

147
00:34:37.408 --> 00:34:39.243
<i>She had to improvise.</i>

148
00:34:49.170 --> 00:34:55.426
<i>I studied her every move</i>
<i>as she stalked them silently.</i>

149
00:35:10.441 --> 00:35:12.318
<i>But once her cover was blown,</i>

150
00:35:13.069 --> 00:35:18.699
<i>it became a game of chase that</i>
<i>we were never going to win.</i>

151
00:35:32.588 --> 00:35:35.049
<i>They swam rings around us.</i>

152
00:36:06.289 --> 00:36:13.212
<i>But Mom somehow was always able to pull</i>
<i>some food out of nowhere.</i>

153
00:36:19.302 --> 00:36:21.304
<i>Seaweed for dinner.</i>

154
00:36:22.471 --> 00:36:25.391
<i>We hated seaweed for dinner.</i>

155
00:36:28.019 --> 00:36:29.979
<i>Especially my brother.</i>

156
00:36:31.314 --> 00:36:36.527
<i>He'd rather go without dinner</i>
<i>than eat seaweed.</i>

157
00:36:41.908 --> 00:36:44.785
(BIRDS CALLING)

158
00:36:46.370 --> 00:36:50.541
<i>As summer dragged on,</i>
<i>food became even more scarce.</i>

159
00:36:51.709 --> 00:36:55.504
<i>It was there,</i>
<i>but it was often very hard to reach.</i>

160
00:36:59.342 --> 00:37:02.637
<i>Birds came to the cliffs every summer</i>
<i>to have their chicks.</i>

161
00:37:06.515 --> 00:37:10.436
<i>They had to nest wherever they could,</i>
<i>to be safe from predators.</i>

162
00:37:22.907 --> 00:37:25.451
<i>Every square inch was precious.</i>

163
00:37:29.038 --> 00:37:30.289
(BIRDS SQUAWKING)

164
00:37:38.506 --> 00:37:42.051
<i>We ice bears will climb</i>
<i>almost anything for food,</i>

165
00:37:42.551 --> 00:37:45.137
<i>and Mom was ready to show us how.</i>

166
00:37:48.599 --> 00:37:51.602
<i>But we weren't the only hungry ones there.</i>

167
00:37:55.064 --> 00:37:58.067
<i>She'd been outdone</i>
<i>by yet another male bear.</i>

168
00:38:11.330 --> 00:38:14.041
<i>The climb was dangerous enough.</i>

169
00:38:14.125 --> 00:38:16.836
<i>Mom wasn't going to attempt it</i>
<i>with him up there.</i>

170
00:38:34.520 --> 00:38:37.064
<i>The cliffs were crumbling</i>
<i>beneath his feet.</i>

171
00:38:51.078 --> 00:38:58.002
<i>Trying to snatch prey that flies on</i>
<i>a dangerous rock face is not an option.</i>

172
00:39:09.889 --> 00:39:12.558
<i>He had to settle for eggs or chicks.</i>

173
00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:42.296
<i>Far below, my brother managed</i>
<i>to catch us a much better meal.</i>

174
00:39:45.132 --> 00:39:47.051
<i>It was our little victory.</i>

175
00:39:59.980 --> 00:40:01.690
<i>Summer was often like this.</i>

176
00:40:02.650 --> 00:40:05.986
<i>Ice bears forced to extremes by hunger.</i>

177
00:40:11.242 --> 00:40:12.868
<i>All for a tiny bite.</i>

178
00:40:27.133 --> 00:40:30.344
<i>All summer ever provided was scraps.</i>

179
00:40:31.137 --> 00:40:34.181
<i>Those who took the risks</i>
<i>were the ones who ate.</i>

180
00:40:40.729 --> 00:40:46.944
<i>The land could provide food,</i>
<i>just not for us. Not this time.</i>

181
00:41:06.422 --> 00:41:09.967
<i>Today, the summers are getting</i>
<i>longer and longer.</i>

182
00:41:25.357 --> 00:41:30.779
<i>What I learned about finding small scraps</i>
<i>in hard times has kept us alive.</i>

183
00:41:47.421 --> 00:41:50.925
<i>But a young ice bear needs to do more</i>
<i>than just survive.</i>

184
00:41:53.928 --> 00:41:55.221
<i>She needs to grow.</i>

185
00:42:20.079 --> 00:42:22.998
<i>I remember, in autumn of that second year,</i>

186
00:42:23.999 --> 00:42:26.919
<i>we had an incredible discovery.</i>

187
00:42:37.346 --> 00:42:40.683
<i>A dead whale washed up on the shore.</i>

188
00:42:49.233 --> 00:42:52.570
<i>This would keep us fed</i>
<i>for a very long time.</i>

189
00:43:02.705 --> 00:43:06.750
<i>But I quickly realized this was not</i>
<i>going to be an easy meal.</i>

190
00:43:09.086 --> 00:43:11.755
<i>Getting through the thick skin</i>
<i>was nearly impossible.</i>

191
00:43:20.222 --> 00:43:24.977
<i>Underneath was so much rich blubber.</i>
<i>I could smell it.</i>

192
00:43:29.064 --> 00:43:31.984
<i>But the trick was getting to it.</i>

193
00:43:40.868 --> 00:43:45.706
<i>Just as we were making some progress,</i>
<i>another male.</i>

194
00:43:46.373 --> 00:43:49.627
<i>Come to ruin our good fortune, again.</i>

195
00:43:53.964 --> 00:43:56.133
<i>It was best to keep our distance.</i>

196
00:44:11.857 --> 00:44:15.861
<i>At least he would be more interested</i>
<i>in the whale than us.</i>

197
00:44:51.730 --> 00:44:53.107
<i>I was so jealous,</i>

198
00:44:53.524 --> 00:44:57.403
<i>watching as he broke through the skin</i>
<i>with his more powerful jaws.</i>

199
00:45:04.243 --> 00:45:09.581
<i>Mom decided this opportunity</i>
<i>was too great to abandon.</i>

200
00:45:12.209 --> 00:45:14.586
<i>Good things come to those who wait.</i>

201
00:45:29.893 --> 00:45:33.689
<i>In the days that followed,</i>
<i>more and more bears arrived,</i>

202
00:45:34.064 --> 00:45:37.025
<i>lured by the smell of the delicious feast.</i>

203
00:45:44.950 --> 00:45:50.706
<i>Mom wasn't letting me anywhere close,</i>
<i>until they were all well fed.</i>

204
00:45:55.419 --> 00:45:59.298
<i>It didn't take long for all those jaws</i>
<i>to tear through the skin</i>

205
00:45:59.381 --> 00:46:03.093
<i>and gorge on the juicy goodness inside.</i>

206
00:46:14.271 --> 00:46:17.065
<i>I so wanted in on that.</i>

207
00:46:32.498 --> 00:46:33.957
<i>Once they'd had their fill,</i>

208
00:46:34.374 --> 00:46:37.753
<i>they all washed off their sloppy meal</i>
<i>with a nice swim.</i>

209
00:46:46.887 --> 00:46:51.600
<i>I had never seen so many ice bears</i>
<i>together in one place.</i>

210
00:46:56.772 --> 00:47:03.278
<i>In that moment, with so much food</i>
<i>to go around, there was no competition.</i>

211
00:47:04.530 --> 00:47:07.616
<i>So they simply reveled</i>
<i>in each other's company.</i>

212
00:47:14.915 --> 00:47:19.628
<i>Finally, when even the biggest of them</i>
<i>was stuffed completely,</i>

213
00:47:20.420 --> 00:47:22.005
<i>I took my turn.</i>

214
00:47:25.676 --> 00:47:27.678
<i>Way better than seaweed.</i>

215
00:47:37.271 --> 00:47:39.231
<i>After all we'd been through,</i>

216
00:47:42.818 --> 00:47:46.071
<i>all the hunger and hardship,</i>

217
00:47:48.282 --> 00:47:54.079
<i>I can still remember</i>
<i>the three of us just playing.</i>

218
00:48:01.670 --> 00:48:04.840
<i>It was the best day of my life.</i>

219
00:49:05.108 --> 00:49:08.695
<i>Our second winter was much worse</i>
<i>than our first.</i>

220
00:49:17.079 --> 00:49:19.539
<i>The power of those storms...</i>

221
00:49:21.124 --> 00:49:23.001
<i>they were something totally new.</i>

222
00:49:49.945 --> 00:49:54.658
<i>When spring arrived,</i>
<i>there were only two of us.</i>

223
00:50:03.917 --> 00:50:06.044
<i>The winter had taken my brother.</i>

224
00:50:16.430 --> 00:50:18.098
(GROANING)

225
00:50:40.996 --> 00:50:44.916
<i>From then on, it was just Mom and me.</i>

226
00:51:19.618 --> 00:51:26.166
<i>Fire and ice have always been enemies.</i>
<i>But now, fire is winning.</i>

227
00:51:34.966 --> 00:51:38.553
<i>Even the land is beginning to melt</i>
<i>beneath our feet.</i>

228
00:51:49.231 --> 00:51:53.527
<i>The old routes through our home</i>
<i>are becoming impassable.</i>

229
00:52:01.952 --> 00:52:04.246
<i>This is not the summer I knew.</i>

230
00:52:05.664 --> 00:52:09.042
<i>This is some other season.</i>

231
00:52:36.862 --> 00:52:40.574
<i>I remember the third summer</i>
<i>of my childhood was the warmest.</i>

232
00:52:48.123 --> 00:52:50.167
<i>The sea ice melted away early.</i>

233
00:52:50.750 --> 00:52:53.545
<i>And the seals were almost</i>
<i>impossible to find.</i>

234
00:53:02.304 --> 00:53:07.225
<i>So Mom led me to another of her</i>
<i>special places to find food.</i>

235
00:53:13.148 --> 00:53:17.360
<i>The tip of an island,</i>
<i>where a new type of prey I'd never seen</i>

236
00:53:17.444 --> 00:53:19.154
<i>was waiting for us.</i>

237
00:53:22.032 --> 00:53:23.325
<i>Walrus.</i>

238
00:53:32.709 --> 00:53:37.505
<i>I was fascinated by these strange</i>
<i>creatures with the strange teeth.</i>

239
00:53:46.806 --> 00:53:49.768
<i>Or maybe it was "frightened."</i>
<i>I can't remember.</i>

240
00:54:01.947 --> 00:54:04.658
<i>But Mom had a reason for bringing me here.</i>

241
00:54:05.700 --> 00:54:09.788
<i>It was time for me</i>
<i>to try my hand at hunting.</i>

242
00:54:15.877 --> 00:54:19.923
<i>I tried to decide which one would make</i>
<i>the easiest target.</i>

243
00:54:23.635 --> 00:54:25.637
(GROWLS)

244
00:54:27.097 --> 00:54:30.016
<i>I decided none of them.</i>

245
00:54:34.646 --> 00:54:38.858
<i>Mom went up to investigate the walrus</i>
<i>gathered at the top of the beach.</i>

246
00:54:42.862 --> 00:54:46.408
<i>Adults, all tightly packed together.</i>

247
00:54:49.202 --> 00:54:51.496
<i>Too many, and too big to handle.</i>

248
00:54:59.879 --> 00:55:01.631
(BELLOWING)

249
00:55:07.387 --> 00:55:10.932
<i>When she came back down to the water</i>
<i>to see how I was progressing,</i>

250
00:55:11.016 --> 00:55:13.518
<i>I had almost worked out a plan.</i>

251
00:55:19.232 --> 00:55:23.361
<i>Mother walrus, holding their newborn</i>
<i>pups with their flippers.</i>

252
00:55:26.323 --> 00:55:29.284
<i>The perfect-sized prey for us.</i>

253
00:55:34.331 --> 00:55:38.752
<i>Just swimming up and stealing them</i>
<i>from their mothers in the water</i>

254
00:55:38.835 --> 00:55:40.545
<i>was not going to happen.</i>

255
00:55:45.300 --> 00:55:50.430
<i>But maybe there would be some pups hiding</i>
<i>among the adults on the beach.</i>

256
00:56:09.366 --> 00:56:13.661
<i>There were, tucked in around</i>
<i>the edge of the huddle.</i>

257
00:56:19.042 --> 00:56:20.627
<i>I took up my position.</i>

258
00:56:23.088 --> 00:56:25.006
<i>They didn't seem to care.</i>

259
00:56:27.467 --> 00:56:31.262
<i>It wasn't until Mom moved in</i>
<i>and created panic</i>

260
00:56:31.346 --> 00:56:33.765
<i>that they started moving into the water.</i>

261
00:56:36.017 --> 00:56:37.852
(WALRUSES GRUNTING)

262
00:56:54.285 --> 00:56:55.453
<i>It worked.</i>

263
00:56:56.162 --> 00:56:59.040
<i>A pup, left behind by a panicked mother.</i>

264
00:57:23.898 --> 00:57:27.152
<i>It was the best meal we'd had in ages.</i>

265
00:57:28.945 --> 00:57:32.031
<i>And I was finally taking</i>
<i>a bigger role in hunting.</i>

266
00:57:48.798 --> 00:57:52.594
<i>Just as winter was setting in</i>
<i>that third year,</i>

267
00:57:52.677 --> 00:57:54.637
<i>my life changed forever.</i>

268
00:58:05.190 --> 00:58:09.027
<i>Mom knew it was time for me</i>
<i>to make my own way.</i>

269
00:58:14.699 --> 00:58:17.285
<i>She had taught me everything she could.</i>

270
00:58:17.911 --> 00:58:19.996
<i>So, she let me go.</i>

271
00:58:38.681 --> 00:58:43.353
<i>Everything I'd learned from her,</i>
<i>I would now have to attempt on my own.</i>

272
00:59:02.413 --> 00:59:04.082
<i>It was frightening.</i>

273
00:59:05.124 --> 00:59:08.503
<i>The world had never seemed</i>
<i>so vast and lonely.</i>

274
00:59:36.823 --> 00:59:40.243
<i>I didn't know if I could survive</i>
<i>without her.</i>

275
01:00:10.565 --> 01:00:13.860
<i>I wandered alone for the next three years.</i>

276
01:00:18.906 --> 01:00:22.869
<i>I did not encounter another ice bear</i>
<i>in all that time.</i>

277
01:01:02.617 --> 01:01:04.452
<i>I wasn't really alone, though.</i>

278
01:01:08.456 --> 01:01:09.832
<i>She was with me.</i>

279
01:01:17.090 --> 01:01:19.842
<i>She was a part of every experience,</i>

280
01:01:21.761 --> 01:01:23.221
<i>every decision,</i>

281
01:01:26.724 --> 01:01:28.017
<i>every journey.</i>

282
01:01:33.606 --> 01:01:36.734
<i>A part of the bear that I had become.</i>

283
01:01:42.782 --> 01:01:47.995
<i>Her knowledge is what got me through</i>
<i>those three long, grueling winters.</i>

284
01:02:23.823 --> 01:02:28.953
<i>And then that spring,</i>
<i>something extraordinary happened.</i>

285
01:02:38.254 --> 01:02:40.006
<i>I met another ice bear.</i>

286
01:02:46.095 --> 01:02:50.266
<i>My experience with male bears</i>
<i>made me very cautious.</i>

287
01:02:51.350 --> 01:02:53.936
<i>But that old fear quickly vanished.</i>

288
01:02:56.439 --> 01:02:58.024
<i>He was friendly.</i>

289
01:03:04.405 --> 01:03:08.910
<i>We were the same age and had both</i>
<i>been on our own for so long.</i>

290
01:03:09.911 --> 01:03:13.664
<i>We just played together</i>
<i>like carefree cubs the whole day.</i>

291
01:03:23.132 --> 01:03:25.134
<i>We ran off to my favorite spot.</i>

292
01:03:28.888 --> 01:03:32.558
<i>The ice edge,</i>
<i>where I used to play with my brother.</i>

293
01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:35.937
(PLAYFUL GROWLING)

294
01:04:43.838 --> 01:04:45.548
(GRUNTING)

295
01:05:18.706 --> 01:05:24.879
<i>That day, I realized</i>
<i>not all male bears had to be feared.</i>

296
01:06:01.707 --> 01:06:05.127
<i>Just as suddenly as he'd arrived,</i>
<i>he was on his way again.</i>

297
01:06:08.714 --> 01:06:12.802
<i>We were just two young bears</i>
<i>who met one day</i>

298
01:06:12.885 --> 01:06:15.054
<i>in the middle of the boundless ice.</i>

299
01:06:29.944 --> 01:06:35.157
<i>Later that spring, my newfound confidence</i>
<i>would be truly tested.</i>

300
01:06:45.835 --> 01:06:50.631
<i>A massive, full-grown male,</i>
<i>more than twice my size.</i>

301
01:07:05.813 --> 01:07:07.606
<i>He followed my scent,</i>

302
01:07:08.899 --> 01:07:11.527
<i>and tracked my footsteps in the snow.</i>

303
01:07:51.233 --> 01:07:54.320
<i>For days, he shadowed my every move.</i>

304
01:08:12.838 --> 01:08:16.467
<i>I had been running from male bears</i>
<i>my whole life.</i>

305
01:08:18.803 --> 01:08:22.306
<i>But something about this was different.</i>

306
01:08:25.017 --> 01:08:26.727
<i>I felt a strength.</i>

307
01:08:33.526 --> 01:08:35.194
<i>I wasn't scared.</i>

308
01:09:13.691 --> 01:09:18.320
<i>I soon understood I was being courted.</i>

309
01:09:52.521 --> 01:09:55.399
<i>He stayed by my side for many days.</i>

310
01:09:56.233 --> 01:09:59.653
<i>Until finally, I felt the time was right.</i>

311
01:10:05.701 --> 01:10:09.788
<i>I wanted no trouble from</i>
<i>any interfering ice bears,</i>

312
01:10:09.872 --> 01:10:15.252
<i>so I led him far away from the sea ice,</i>
<i>into the mountains.</i>

313
01:10:26.472 --> 01:10:29.266
<i>It was a long, tiring trek,</i>

314
01:10:29.558 --> 01:10:33.437
<i>and we had to stop to rest</i>
<i>before we reached the summit.</i>

315
01:10:44.573 --> 01:10:46.533
<i>We fell asleep together.</i>

316
01:10:51.705 --> 01:10:54.792
<i>I knew I could trust him.</i>

317
01:11:12.226 --> 01:11:17.022
<i>Above the clouds, not far from</i>
<i>the very cave where I was born,</i>

318
01:11:18.190 --> 01:11:22.319
<i>he would help provide me</i>
<i>with the only thing I truly desired</i>

319
01:11:22.444 --> 01:11:24.488
<i>since parting with my family.</i>

320
01:11:25.698 --> 01:11:28.284
<i>A family of my own.</i>

321
01:11:47.344 --> 01:11:49.221
<i>I would never see him again.</i>

322
01:11:53.225 --> 01:11:56.729
<i>But the next spring, my wish came true.</i>

323
01:11:58.397 --> 01:12:00.316
<i>I had a cub of my own.</i>

324
01:12:14.163 --> 01:12:15.289
<i>Just one.</i>

325
01:12:15.956 --> 01:12:18.250
<i>But that made her all the more special.</i>

326
01:12:49.198 --> 01:12:51.909
<i>She so reminded me of my brother.</i>

327
01:13:39.790 --> 01:13:44.378
<i>Nursing my own cub,</i>
<i>looking back on my childhood,</i>

328
01:13:45.295 --> 01:13:49.049
<i>I felt I had come full circle.</i>

329
01:13:49.174 --> 01:13:55.013
<i>And that despite all the challenges,</i>
<i>I had succeeded.</i>

330
01:13:57.182 --> 01:13:59.643
<i>My mother had succeeded.</i>

331
01:14:39.766 --> 01:14:43.187
<i>We ice bears are great survivors.</i>

332
01:15:03.874 --> 01:15:07.336
<i>We have always mastered</i>
<i>the changes we have faced.</i>

333
01:15:21.391 --> 01:15:26.813
<i>We have done so by carrying the knowledge</i>
<i>of those who've gone before.</i>

334
01:15:36.949 --> 01:15:38.450
<i>Where to find ice.</i>

335
01:15:44.623 --> 01:15:46.500
<i>How to find food.</i>

336
01:15:54.591 --> 01:15:58.387
<i>How to adapt to an evolving landscape.</i>

337
01:16:18.031 --> 01:16:22.077
<i>But I am reaching the limits</i>
<i>of what I know about this world.</i>

338
01:16:31.211 --> 01:16:36.049
<i>These new changes seem to me</i>
<i>almost insurmountable.</i>

339
01:17:00.073 --> 01:17:05.579
<i>My daughter will learn what it takes</i>
<i>to be a great ice bear.</i>

340
01:17:21.345 --> 01:17:23.305
<i>She will endure.</i>

341
01:17:37.819 --> 01:17:41.573
<i>But what kind of world will she call home?</i>
